---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/docs/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/docs/Callout.astro';
import PrevNext from '../../../components/docs/PrevNext.astro';
import { url } from '../../../utils/paths';
---

<DocsLayout title="/codegraph:init">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-4">/codegraph:init</h1>
  <p class="text-xl text-text-secondary mb-8">
    Installs the plugin's native dependencies. Run this once before indexing.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mt-10 mb-4">Overview</h2>
  <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
    The <code class="bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-1 rounded text-primary">/codegraph:init</code> command installs
    the LadybugDB graph engine and the tree-sitter grammars into the plugin's data directory. These are
    native modules that cannot be bundled, so they are installed on your machine the first time you set up
    the plugin. The MCP server and the indexer both load them from that directory.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mt-10 mb-4">What it does</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-text-secondary space-y-2 mb-6">
    <li>Installs the embedded graph engine (<code class="text-primary">@ladybugdb/core</code>) and the tree-sitter parsers</li>
    <li>Places them in the plugin's persistent data directory, kept across plugin updates</li>
    <li>Downloads a prebuilt binary for your platform when one exists, and compiles from source otherwise</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mt-10 mb-4">Usage</h2>
  <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
    Run it once, right after installing the plugin:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    code="/codegraph:init"
    lang="bash"
    title="Claude Code"
  />

  <Callout type="warning" title="Reconnect required after init">
    The MCP server reads its dependencies when its process starts, and Claude Code does not reconnect a
    stdio server on its own. After <code class="bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-primary">/codegraph:init</code>,
    reconnect <strong>codegraph</strong> from the <code class="bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-primary">/mcp</code>
    panel (restarting Claude Code works too, but is not required).
  </Callout>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mt-10 mb-4">When to run it</h2>
  <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-text-secondary space-y-2 mb-6">
    <li>Once, after installing the plugin</li>
    <li>Again after a plugin update that changes dependencies</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
    Re-running it when nothing changed is harmless: npm reports everything up to date and leaves the
    installation alone.
  </p>

  <Callout type="tip" title="Starting over">
    Wiping the plugin's data directory resets the installation. Run <code class="bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-primary">/codegraph:init</code>
    again afterwards, and <code class="bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-primary">/codegraph:index</code> too if you removed the graph file.
  </Callout>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mt-10 mb-4">Troubleshooting</h2>
  <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
    If <code class="bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-1 rounded text-primary">npm</code> fails during init, the cause is
    almost always a missing build toolchain for the native modules, not the plugin itself. Report the npm
    output as-is. A session-start warning that the native dependencies are missing means the same thing:
    run <code class="bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-primary">/codegraph:init</code>, then reconnect
    codegraph from <code class="bg-bg-subtle px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-primary">/mcp</code>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text-primary mt-10 mb-4">Next Steps</h2>
  <p class="text-text-secondary mb-4">
    Once the dependencies are installed and codegraph is reconnected, index your project with the
    <a href={url('/docs/commands/index-cmd')} class="text-primary hover:text-secondary underline">/codegraph:index</a> command.
  </p>

  <PrevNext
    prev={{ title: "MCP Standalone", href: "/docs/installation/mcp-standalone" }}
    next={{ title: "/codegraph:index", href: "/docs/commands/index-cmd" }}
  />
</DocsLayout>
